WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.540
Next LC-36A, tower module addition moves, Florida starship operations closer to first flights. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 139. A super heavy booster heads for a hold-down firing, starship missions move in parallel, and Kennedy Space Center is asked for more land. Plus the engineering deep dive, construction crews at the historic Florida Complex are integrating the new section into the existing tower during the rebuild, according to site video on YouTube.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.320
The lift is in progress and it follows foundation and base work completed in recent

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:40.332
weeks. Booster 22 is heading to pad 2 tonight for a potential weekend static fire test. Road

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:46.492
delays are scheduled between 11.59 pm and 4 am central daylight time. The move puts the

00:00:46.492 --> 00:00:51.472
booster on the test stand so teams can verify propellant loading and engine ignition sequences.

00:00:52.032 --> 00:00:57.272
They will watch data from all 33 Raptor engines during the planned hold down firing, with

00:00:57.272 --> 00:01:02.332
the vehicle bolted to the stand. Any issues found feed straight into pre-flight checks for the

00:01:02.332 --> 00:01:09.998
upcoming mission. SpaceX has Flight 15 targeted for mid-November from pad 2. Flight 16 hardware is

00:01:09.998 --> 00:01:16.518
preparing to move to Kennedy Space Center, or KSC, for a launch from 39A. The dual-flow approach

00:01:16.518 --> 00:01:21.678
lets teams ready to complete stacks at the same time. Booster and ship hardware for each flight

00:01:21.678 --> 00:01:26.878
follow separate processing paths at Starbase and the Cape. The schedule is meant to keep both

00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:32.498
missions on track despite shared infrastructure. Ground crews at each site are coordinating timelines

00:01:32.498 --> 00:01:38.492
to avoid resource conflicts. Kennedy Space Center is the site of a SpaceX request for more land

00:01:38.492 --> 00:01:43.992
to support advancing starship operations, the Business Journal's report. The company is asking

00:01:43.992 --> 00:01:49.712
for 400 acres that would add vehicle processing buildings and support facilities. Current KSC

00:01:49.712 --> 00:01:55.052
infrastructure is nearing capacity with multiple programs running in parallel. Approval would let

00:01:55.052 --> 00:01:57.092
construction start before the end of the year.

00:01:57.712 --> 00:02:01.912
The expansion lines up with earlier announcements about a higher flight cadence from the Cape.

00:02:02.782 --> 00:02:07.922
The Space Force has reassigned six national security launches to SpaceX, according to a

00:02:07.922 --> 00:02:09.882
Reddit post that remains unconfirmed.

00:02:10.282 --> 00:02:12.942
The shift came while the Vulcan rocket stays grounded.

00:02:13.482 --> 00:02:18.182
Mission manifests now root those payloads onto Falcon 9 vehicles already in the production

00:02:18.182 --> 00:02:18.542
queue.

00:02:19.102 --> 00:02:23.802
The change increases pressure on existing booster reuse cycles at both Vandenberg and

00:02:23.802 --> 00:02:24.142
the Cape.

00:02:24.142 --> 00:02:29.142
contract adjustments are expected to reflect the new launch dates. Space Force

00:02:29.142 --> 00:02:34.149
officials cited schedule certainty as the primary driver, unfavorable weather

00:02:34.149 --> 00:02:39.089
forced to stand down of a planned star-linked mission. SpaceX set on X. The next

00:02:39.089 --> 00:02:44.169
opportunity is no earlier than Friday, October 23rd. Range safety officers

00:02:44.169 --> 00:02:47.869
recorded shifting upper-level winds and lightning risk in the launch corridor.

00:02:48.329 --> 00:02:53.689
The 27 satellite stack remains secured on the pad at Vandenberg. Recovery teams

00:02:53.689 --> 00:02:59.333
will run additional checks once the window reopens. Elon Musk recommended Grokbot for

00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:04.713
almost any personal or business task. He described it as a life and business manager equivalent

00:03:04.713 --> 00:03:09.993
to having a genius employee. The recommendation points to recent gains in task handling and

00:03:09.993 --> 00:03:15.413
context retention. Follow-up posts stressed reliability for scheduling, research, and routine

00:03:15.413 --> 00:03:21.752
decisions. Early adopters report measurable time savings on repetitive workflows. Memphis

00:03:21.752 --> 00:03:26.352
Memphis is holding Musk for nights and days as the SI project fuels SpaceX expansion,

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:28.292
the commercial appeal reports.

00:03:28.852 --> 00:03:32.112
The data center worked ties directly to revenue growth for the company.

00:03:32.732 --> 00:03:37.112
Local infrastructure upgrades are accelerating to handle higher power and cooling loads.

00:03:37.612 --> 00:03:41.492
Project timelines now include round-the-clock oversight from senior leadership.

00:03:42.132 --> 00:03:46.372
Revenue from these facilities is already showing up in quarterly results reported earlier

00:03:46.372 --> 00:03:46.952
this month.

00:03:46.952 --> 00:03:52.765
Elsewhere, a Texas Environmental Review could set precedence for how SpaceX projects are

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:56.345
assessed in Louisiana, according to the Louisiana Illuminator.

00:03:56.945 --> 00:04:01.665
XAI launched a SpaceX Super Intelligence Partner Network that connects partners to growing

00:04:01.665 --> 00:04:03.725
compute and intelligence infrastructure.

00:04:04.748 --> 00:04:09.308
Users on Reddit's SpaceX Lounge are sharing photos of Starship Mission Patch collections

00:04:09.308 --> 00:04:11.768
covering every flight test through flight 14.

00:04:11.768 --> 00:04:18.668
Those collections mix official SpaceX patches with NASA's spaceflight editions obtained when shipping costs were lower.

00:04:19.328 --> 00:04:26.888
Community members on X are trying GROC BOT for daily scheduling and research and reporting quick replies on both personal and technical questions.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:33.840
Worth keeping an eye on is a Houston Chronicle opinion arguing that Boca Chica State Parkland should remain public.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.340
The column tells Elon Musk the state will not simply hand that acreage over.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:43.820
It frames the talks as a test of whether private space development can override established public

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:47.900
access rights without stronger environmental and community safeguards.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:53.040
Resolution would take either legislation or a negotiated settlement that satisfies both

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:56.080
park advocates and SpaceX infrastructure needs.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:01.320
Local stakeholders keep pressing for more studies on habitat and public recreation impacts

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.940
before any transfer proceeds.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:11.207
Starship propellant, from an engineering standpoint, only beats Falcon 9 economics after the vehicle reaches high flight rates.

00:05:11.627 --> 00:05:16.687
A full stack holds roughly 4,600 to 5,100 tons of propellant.

00:05:17.087 --> 00:05:23.787
One Falcon 9 tanks about 490 to 515 tons, so 10 of those flights burn a similar mass.

00:05:23.787 --> 00:05:29.047
One half-loaded starship on flight 14 already equaled the work of about 10 Falcon

00:05:29.047 --> 00:05:35.587
9 V2 mini-flights, carrying 26 V3 Starlink satellites rated at roughly 1 terabit per second

00:05:35.587 --> 00:05:41.107
a piece. At full load, the gap widens, because both stages are designed to fly again, and

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:45.667
the vehicle can put up to 20 times Falcon 9's orbital mass on a comparable propellant

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:51.067
burn. Reuse spreads the same tanks and fuel over many flights until the rate is high,

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:55.467
those tons do not yet mean cheaper satellites. Oxygen and methane are

00:05:55.467 --> 00:06:00.047
liquefied from electricity and feedstock, so cost per ton tracks power price

00:06:00.047 --> 00:06:05.587
and plant hours, not scarce ore. A back-of-envelope figure for air separation is on

00:06:05.587 --> 00:06:11.367
the order of 0.4 to 1 kilowatt hour per kilogram of liquid oxygen, with methane via

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:16.207
hydrogen adding more through electrolysis. Kinetic energy to low Earth orbit is

00:06:16.207 --> 00:06:20.887
about 30 megajoules per kilogram. Gravity and drag mean the chemical energy you

00:06:20.887 --> 00:06:24.587
burn is several times that, which is why the tanks dwarf the payload.

00:06:25.207 --> 00:06:26.947
The rocket equation is unforgiving.

00:06:27.527 --> 00:06:31.747
Most of the propellant exists to lift the rest of the propellant, so throwing stage is

00:06:31.747 --> 00:06:33.707
a way multiplies the metal you pay for.

00:06:34.247 --> 00:06:39.447
Ten Falcon 9 flights spread that energy across ten vehicles and ten ground crews, while

00:06:39.447 --> 00:06:42.987
one starship flight pours it into a single stack and a single pad.

00:06:43.587 --> 00:06:48.607
Once the super heavy booster and the ship both return and fly again within days, tower,

00:06:48.607 --> 00:06:51.707
poor pad and factory stop dominating the Perflight bill.

00:06:52.187 --> 00:06:56.547
On a generic rocket, dry structure might be on the order of a tenth of the fueled mass.

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:59.467
Discard it and you buy a new tenth every flight.

00:06:59.967 --> 00:07:04.367
But fly that metal a hundred times, and a back of envelope split puts the structure near

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:05.627
1% Perflight.

00:07:06.147 --> 00:07:08.007
That is the idiot index in launch.

00:07:08.567 --> 00:07:13.207
The finished satellite costs many times the raw propellant and metal, because expendable

00:07:13.207 --> 00:07:14.347
hardware ate the money.

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:17.187
A rough estimate is tens of times those inputs.

00:07:17.767 --> 00:07:23.227
Starship drives that ratio down by reusing both stages and flying often enough that overhead

00:07:23.227 --> 00:07:24.587
per flight becomes small.

00:07:25.067 --> 00:07:30.847
When one stack flies as many times in a year as 10 Falcon 9 boosters combined, the propellant

00:07:30.847 --> 00:07:34.127
math becomes a lower cost for every kilogram placed in orbit.

00:07:34.647 --> 00:07:36.827
The stock closed higher, up 2%.

00:07:36.827 --> 00:07:43.112
Before we go, if tonight's road closure holds, booster 22 could be on the pad to stand

00:07:43.112 --> 00:07:44.532
for a weekend static fire.

00:07:45.012 --> 00:07:46.732
That's your SpaceX news for today.

